PATCH 363: mission per-object display-list LIFECYCLE cluster -- the DAT_2000_9fbc object-slot table
(DGROUP:0xdfbc, 182 entries, STRIDE 4; each nonzero slot is a DGROUP near-offset to an object struct)
base-loss family, asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00).  Four leaf/helper
methods dispatched from the c0e5 per-frame object walk (patch 243) read a slot as a HOST pointer instead
of a DGROUP near-offset:

  FUN_1000_b2d3 @0x1b2d3  set-state:   mov di,[bx-0x2044]; mov word[di],0x13; or byte[di+0x16],1; ...
  FUN_0000_c0ba @0xc0ba   lifetime:    dec byte[di+0x17]; if 0 -> b354(di) -> b2ef
  FUN_1000_b354 @0x1b354  find-index:  si=0xdfbc; cmp word[si],di; si+=4; loop   (Ghidra strode int*+8, int-cmp)
  FUN_1000_b2ef @0x1b2ef  destroy:     or byte[di+0x16],1; clear slot; dec 0xdfbe; remove from a2f7/a38d live-list

On native the small near-offset used as a host pointer lands in unmapped low memory -> SIGSEGV once the
mission sim reaches the object-roster phase (c0e5 -> c0ba -> b354/b2ef, and c0e5 -> ... -> b2d3).  On wasm
the same 16-bit address is inside linear memory so the writes SILENTLY CORRUPT DGROUP -> the display-list
object state is wrong -> the FUN_0000_20d6 child-walk dispatches wild method offsets -> the extender op-0x50
projection loop spins ~1241x -> recursive FUN_0000_2486 stack overflow (the wasm mission-render blocker).
Same root, two symptoms.

FIX: rebase every object near-offset to g_mem+0x1c000+off (the DGROUP base) and restore the asm field
widths/strides (b354: word compare + stride-4; b2ef: byte[di+0x16], word[di+2] subindex).  The table reads
(&DAT_2000_9fbc = g_mem+0x29fbc = DGROUP:0xdfbc; &DAT_2000_9fbe the adjacent counter) are already correctly
based -- only the near-offset's use as a pointer was wrong.  Same class + fix pattern as the c0e5 walk
(patch 243) and patches 335-340.  Behaviour-neutral for the 28 verify flows (mission-object path only).
